<title>GEORGIA: TENNIS-GEORGIA BEAT NIGERIA 5-0 IN DAVIS CUP PLAY-OFF.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-GEORGIA BEAT NIGERIA 5-0 IN DAVIS CUP PLAY-OFF.</headline>
<dateline>TBILISI 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Georgia beat Nigeria 5-0 in</p>
<p>their Davis Cup tennis Euro/African Zone group two play-off</p>
<p>after winning the reverse singles on Monday.</p>
<p>Rain washed out play on Sunday and the final matches were</p>
<p>reduced to the best of three sets.</p>
<p>Monday's results (Georgian names first):</p>
<p>Givi Samkharadze beat Sule Ladipo 6-3 (Ladipo abandoned match</p>
<p>after first set).</p>
<p>Vladimir Margalitadze beat Jean-Louis Abelekan 6-1 6-2.</p>
</text>
